-NetScript workspace by installing the official **`auth`** plugin. You will choose an authentication
-backend, run the auth database migration, set the backend's environment, and verify a live session
-through the `auth-api` service on **`:8094`**. By the end you have a working OAuth/OIDC sign-in flow
-on the default backend (`kv-oauth`) and a clear picture of what the two non-interactive backends
-(`workos`, `better-auth`) do and do not provide.
