+## Summary
+
+This PR removes the auth plugin's collision with consumer Prisma model names, makes plugin schema
+merges reject different-body declarations and deduplicate identical ones, and promotes decisive
+production E2E errors into the GitHub annotation and step summary.
+
+The real cause of #1058 is a name collision between two different models: the scaffold example
+`User` generated by `--service-name users`, and better-auth's plugin model `User`. It is not a
+duplicated fetched fragment.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Archetypes / areas: CLI/tooling, plugin, auth integration, database diagnostics
+- Refs #1058
+
+## Remaining scope
+
+Acceptance criterion 1 remains: `database.init` passes in `e2e-cli-prod.yml` against a published
+canary CLI. A published canary cannot exist until after merge; the orchestrator will dispatch that
+post-merge gate.
+
+## Diagnosis and hypothesis refutation
+
+Both hypotheses recorded on #1058 are refuted:
+
+1. **The published fragment was not fetched or written twice.** Published CLI install wrote exactly
+   one file, `database/postgres/schema/plugins/auth/auth.prisma`.
+2. **Fetched fragments were not merged in addition to a duplicate scaffold fragment.** The complete
+   schema tree had five declarations and exactly two `model User` declarations in different files:
+   the scaffold base and the single auth fragment. `fetchJsrPackageSchemaFragments` behaved
+   correctly.
+
+Pre-change reproduction:
+
+```sh
+deno run -A --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli@0.0.3-canary.3 init e2eproj \
+  --path <dir> --db postgres --service --service-name users --service-port 3001 \
+  --ci --yes --no-git --force
+cd <dir>/e2eproj
+deno run -A --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli@0.0.3-canary.3 \
+  plugin install auth --name auth --project-root . --no-samples --force
+grep -rn '^model ' database/postgres/schema/
+```
+
+```text
+database/postgres/schema/plugins/auth/auth.prisma:2:model User {
+database/postgres/schema/plugins/auth/auth.prisma:17:model Session {
+database/postgres/schema/plugins/auth/auth.prisma:33:model Account {
+database/postgres/schema/plugins/auth/auth.prisma:55:model Verification {
+database/postgres/schema/schema.prisma:17:model User {
+```
+
